course: dictionary
lesson: 8083
title: Remarks, big and small
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A remark is something you say or write about someone or something, usually short. In the story, Alice snaps «Nobody asked your opinion», and that short sentence is a remark. Look at the words around it to see what kind of remark it is.
explain: As a verb, to remark means to say what you think or notice. Toad appeared «remarking what a pleasant easy life it was», so he was saying out loud how nice his life was. The words after remarking tell you what he said.
explain: Remarks can be kind or unkind. «Your hair wants cutting» is a rude remark about someone's looks, which is why Alice tells the Hatter not to make personal remarks. A calm, kind remark like «I think you went one too many, let's count again» keeps a game fair. Clues like sharp, mean or rude tell you a remark is unkind.
fact: A remark is something you say or write, usually short.
fact: As a verb, remark means to say what you think or notice.
fact: Personal remarks are rude comments about someone's looks or身 themselves, and they can hurt feelings.
fact: Teachers write remarks on school reports to say how a pupil is doing.
fact: Useful phrases: make a remark, remark on something, and a passing remark.
exercise: Alice says «Nobody asked your opinion». What is this? | *A remark | A question | A map | A song
exercise: Toad is «remarking what a pleasant easy life it was». What is he doing? | Sleeping under a tree | *Saying what he thinks about his life | Shouting for help | Digging a hole
exercise: Which is a kind remark? | Nobody asked your opinion | Your hair wants cutting | Sit down and be quiet | *I think you went one too many, let's count again
test: Tanner's mum and dad make little sharp, mean remarks. What kind of remarks are these? | Kind remarks | *Unkind remarks | Remarks written in a book | Remarks about the weather
test: What does it mean to remark on something? | To hide it | To forget it | *To say what you think or notice about it | To run away from it
exam: Alice tells the Hatter not to make personal remarks. Which of these is a personal remark? | Nice weather for a walk today | Thank you for the tea | Let's go to the park after lunch | *Your hair wants cutting
